{"_id":"68a736358ec3d8323af1dcd2","nodeId":"Hu1jf46OpX44nam_UvYqc","roadmapSlug":"rust","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:32.844Z","description":"# String\n\nRust's `String` is a growable, mutable, UTF-8 encoded string type stored on the heap. Unlike string slices (`&str`), `String` owns its data and can be modified. Create with `String::from(\"text\")` or `\"text\".to_string()`. Common operations include `push_str()`, `push()`, and concatenation with `+` or `format!()` macro.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"String","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/string/struct.String.html","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd8f"},{"type":"official","title":"str","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/primitive.str.html","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd90"},{"type":"official","title":"What as a String?","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch08-02-strings.html?highlight=String#what-is-a-string","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd91"},{"type":"article","title":"Rust String (With Examples)","url":"https://www.programiz.com/rust/string","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd92"},{"type":"video","title":"All Rust string types explained","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CpvzeyzgQdw&pp=ygUOc3RyaW5nIGluIHJ1c3Q%3D","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd93"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:07:02.070Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/rust/content/Hu1jf46OpX44nam_UvYqc.md"}